= Abstract

This is a proposal report for the design and implementation of an *Intelligent Parking Billing System using YOLO and Optical Character Recognition (OCR)*. Intelligent parking systems are a key component of modern smart-city infrastructure, enabling automated vehicle identification, efficient space utilization, and contactless billing. By leveraging YOLO for real-time vehicle and license plate detection and OCR for text recognition, the system aims to accurately monitor parking duration and generate billing without human intervention. Currently, many parking facilities rely on manual processes or sensor-heavy solutions, which are costly, error-prone, and difficult to scale. The lack of a vision-based, software-driven parking billing system limits the efficiency and adaptability of intelligent transportation and urban mobility solutions. 

\
 We have successfully tested vehicle detection and license plate recognition in a controlled environment using YOLO and OCR models. Core functionalities such as vehicle entry detection, license plate extraction, and text recognition have been validated with promising accuracy. We have also established the data processing pipeline and implemented preliminary billing logic based on detected entry and exit timestamps. These steps pave the way for integrating real-time video input and automated billing modules. Beyond these visible developments, we have gained substantial insight into computer vision model deployment, dataset preparation, system integration, and performance optimization, which form a strong foundation for completing the full system implementation.


